{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 27, :comments ["<b>Write for yourself these words</b> — He commanded that he write a book of the covenant and read it in the ears of the people, and that they accept it upon themselves with \"we will do and we will hear,\" as they did the first time (Exodus Rabbah 47:2), for everything that was on the first tablets He intended to renew with them on the second tablets. And there is no doubt that he did so, but Scripture did not trouble to elaborate and say \"and Moses did so,\" as I have shown you in many places (above 10:2, and elsewhere). And the correct interpretation in my eyes is that because Israel are the ones who sinned and transgressed the covenant, the Holy One, blessed be He, needed to renew for them a new covenant that He would not break His covenant with them. And He said to Moses that he should write the conditions; and this is the meaning of <b>for according to the mouth of these words I have made a covenant with you and with Israel</b>. And the meaning of <b>with you</b> is: for your sake I have acted with them, and they were not required to bring themselves into the commitment of this covenant; rather, He, blessed be He, found it necessary to make a covenant with them through the forgiveness that He forgave them, and He wrote down the forgiveness and the conditions."], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 34, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:21:49.455671680Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}